<article class="env-proposition" id="0G51">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G51">Proposition <span data-tag="0G51">48.32.2</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0F42" data-tag="0F42">48.16.1</a> let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of $\textit{FTS}_ S$. Then the functors $Rf_!$ and $f^!$ are adjoint in the following sense: for all $K \in D^ b_{\textit{Coh}}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ and $L \in D^+_{\textit{Coh}}(\mathcal{O}_ Y)$ we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ X(K, f^!L) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\text{Pro-}D^+_{\textit{Coh}}(\mathcal{O}_ Y)}(Rf_!K, L)  \]
</div>
  <p> bifunctorially in $K$ and $L$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose a compactification $j : X \to \overline{X}$ over $Y$ and denote $\overline{f} : \overline{X} \to Y$ the structure morphism. Then we have 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \begin{align*}  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ X(K, f^!L) &  = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ X(K, j^*\overline{f}{}^!L) \\ &  = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\text{Pro-}D^+_{\textit{Coh}}(\mathcal{O}_{\overline{X}})} (Rj_!K, \overline{f}{}^!L) \\ &  = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\text{Pro-}D^+_{\textit{Coh}}(\mathcal{O}_ Y)}(Rf_*Rj_!K, L) \\ &  = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\text{Pro-}D^+_{\textit{Coh}}(\mathcal{O}_ Y)}(Rf_!K, L) \end{align*}
</div>
    <p>
       The first equality follows immediately from the construction of $f^!$ in Section <a href="/tag/0A9Y" data-tag="0A9Y">48.16</a>. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0AU1" data-tag="0AU1">48.17.6</a> we have $\overline{f}{}^!L$ in $D^+_{\textit{Coh}}(\mathcal{O}_{\overline{X}})$ hence the second equality follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0G4K" data-tag="0G4K">48.30.2</a>. Since $\overline{f}$ is proper the functor $\overline{f}{}^!$ is the right adjoint of pushforward by construction. This is why we have the third equality. The fourth equality holds because $Rf_! = Rf_* Rj_!$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>